From 6b93fc111a75ed7b44aea22193d5bef24577301c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: autoresearch <agent@localhost>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 05:48:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] point the ggml gitlink at the tree that was actually
 measured

The submodule pointer still named the pre-session ggml commit while the worktree carried the two bit-identical
CPU fixes, so crispasr reported itself dirty and any checkout or submodule update here would have silently
reverted them. deps.lock in the composite project now records all three dependency heads and the build refuses
to run against anything else.
---
 ggml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml b/ggml
index 2f5a80d..32d6394 160000
--- a/ggml
+++ b/ggml
@@ -1 +1 @@
-Subproject commit 2f5a80d258c46e6ac8eee95f1328c0f58376d7ee
+Subproject commit 32d6394369582d550a278c036588cb374baf1e0c
-- 
2.53.0

